    "body": "claimed: M5 session (Claude) · 2026-11-10T06:01Z · branch issue/672-plasma-laws (stacked on #674; it waits for #670's op shape) · plan: a `plasma_laws` module that judges a plasma program from its CL alone, so it doesn't depend on #670's internals:\n- **Contours:** the cut contours, read from the torch-on spans between M200/G16-style cut starts and M205;\n- **Kerf crossing:** a cut that crosses an earlier cut's kerf band is warned, naming the contour and point;\n- **Cut order:** an inner contour cut after the outer that encloses it is refused by name;\n- **Rapids:** a rapid across a freed part's area is warned (tip-up);\n- **2D gouge:** the kerf band against the part's 2D section.\n\nThe program verdict blocks the post on a refusal, and the machine check's `notes` say these laws judge plasma ops.",
